#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197985 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/id #uuid "985e1b18-0023-55ba-b4e4-69a109d8de58" :question/math-academy-id "e-12485" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/0405639a97f249bbcc4dc18a7eae5b4df24aefb4b4680b569365b3d841c15e6b.png)\n\n   \n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=\\dfrac{y}2$ and $x=y-2$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda(x,y) =\\dfrac y8.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\:\\: 2x \\leq y \\leq x+2 \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/69dcf02cc1883f2b04f81bd6dd486bbe24fedbb813db5778ae3b33ed1fb42e90.png)\n\n     \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x - 2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}(\\frac{y}{8})|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}(\\frac{y}{8})(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}\\frac{y}{8}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}]}_{2x}^{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}((x+2)^{2}-(2x)^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)(4+4x-3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(16-24{x}^{2}+16{x}^{3}-3{x}^{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{[16x-8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4}-\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(32-64+64-\\frac{96}{5})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(\\frac{64}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197986 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/id #uuid "eab955a5-019b-5219-b5d5-32e3818be4b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-12486" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/67d511da69c49e77822011936522f2b236ccc0fa0e0fcd09ce26b428cc8f738a.png)\n\n \n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y=x$ and $y=4x-x^2$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\dfrac92$ square units, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\:\\: x \\leq y \\leq 4x-x^2 \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/6291950b5483f3c102df7249674412c7c11646409cb1b43df604de6bd5ace86f.png)\n\n  \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x - 3|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{2M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{4x-{x}^{2}}|x-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{4x-{x}^{2}}(x-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[y]_{y=x}^{y=4x-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-6x+9)(3x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}-{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-27{x}^{2}+27x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{9{x}^{4}}{4}-9{x}^{3}+\\frac{27{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{{3}^{2}}(-\\frac{{3}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{{3}^{6}}{4}-{3}^{5}+\\frac{{3}^{5}}{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{3}M(-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{3}{4}-1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197988 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4820138b-483c-5ced-8df9-9849f5f2a7cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia Given a Description of a Mass Density Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0f7dbe9f-b448-5e76-9932-68e1ff99904e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12488" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/8ec9b8832f3286032413c4016e88a58a593dfd1b32164e219dc1c2e56e3b0b97.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt x$ and the line $x=1,$ as shown above. \nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt x \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/7faaecf39250dbdd1b92d789f6c217afe883c27533b563dae82ed82d228d9b4d.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x-(-1)| = |x+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda(x,y) = k |y| = ky,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = k y = 4M y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My\\,|x+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2M(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2M\\cdot \\frac{17}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc42c505-27f3-5ee5-a0a5-84b00ecd61e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194352} {:answer/id #uuid "e4103500-e73e-58af-a06c-e42cbcc40130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9M}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194353} {:answer/id #uuid "11e077c3-7d19-5963-9c3b-c2737df6b0ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194354} {:answer/id #uuid "30525621-69e0-58a6-9180-b3ce74192dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194355} {:answer/id #uuid "54d6a489-a12e-5e9b-b1e5-ef14ecb97f30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8M}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11e077c3-7d19-5963-9c3b-c2737df6b0ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194354} :answer-field/id #uuid "c21ac635-708a-5a08-8064-d553a446b635" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9aa46eb-8f5c-53d3-8081-5b060771cd18" :question/math-academy-id "q-163000" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/ed4f595e7613254fd0cb8f27cf0b0f7443cfbe382ab525b0ca8d527c07f528fd.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=\\sqrt{x}$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{1}{3},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/60ec523346df73503dd61893994de6ec31069271b1157f153bbe988c9e694798.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=3M.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}[y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-2x+1)(\\sqrt{x}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5/2}-2{x}^{3/2}+{x}^{1/2}-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{[\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{7/2}-\\frac{4}{5}{x}^{5/2}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3M(\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4820138b-483c-5ced-8df9-9849f5f2a7cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia Given a Description of a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "931466d1-3f1f-597a-b12d-4483277eca8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194364} {:answer/id #uuid "b82712f4-df0c-5fa5-b4ea-63a77af230ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194365} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f61d79-b8d8-5a58-a045-34f877d11e3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194366} {:answer/id #uuid "4570ceff-153a-5f32-b9b8-cfabdc920373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194367} {:answer/id #uuid "47c79474-7535-55c4-8ad2-5d3658d580a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{42M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "931466d1-3f1f-597a-b12d-4483277eca8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194364} :answer-field/id #uuid "59d4667d-aa04-5fc6-a325-94d8cf620f99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "28b15881-bdd0-5404-83c9-3db9be1582eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-163008" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/b48e086ae0e94589d557eceb25b50af9deffdec442cfb7a4e559577bce899c40.png)\n\nA triangular plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $y=2x.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/f040a5500a1415b8617300f34074bb16d895889354ed7e722dbd668a233daebb.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=-2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-(-2)|=|x+2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k|y|=ky,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=ky=\\frac{3M}{2}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\frac{3M}{2}y\\,|x+2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\frac{3M}{2}y(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2)^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2)^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5}+2{x}^{4}+\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}[\\frac{2}{5}+2+\\frac{8}{3}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}[\\frac{76}{15}] \\\\  & =\\frac{38M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cee96a7-25db-5e03-91f4-56d41c2d4209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370603} {:answer/id #uuid "e7801874-73d3-5fd5-9e54-aa1e68f3b041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370604} {:answer/id #uuid "66279535-d7a3-5f4d-80d0-8acee67866a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370605} {:answer/id #uuid "d74e821c-72cc-5f01-bb05-c305e188ad1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370606} {:answer/id #uuid "f8161f00-96b2-521c-b13c-fdee7408fca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d74e821c-72cc-5f01-bb05-c305e188ad1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370606} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8895096-5013-5ba6-bd94-b5c5d5f42e4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9142e89b-aec1-5dd7-a7d7-0241424a0791" :question/math-academy-id "q-163493" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x+y-1$ Find the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y-1)|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-2+y+1)(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-2)^{3}+(y+1)(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{[y(x-2)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(y+1)^{2}(x-2)^{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(x-2)^{3}+\\frac{3}{2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x-2)^{4}}{4}+\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c5329a5-4326-5f4c-9bea-9e93a7ac9902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370610} {:answer/id #uuid "827f65f4-d34d-57b6-b6f4-0992a5931eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{70}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370611} {:answer/id #uuid "973eea0f-0399-52df-be30-a6a313feecd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370612} {:answer/id #uuid "f50076fa-581c-5fdc-8603-c62ba1f8571f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370613} {:answer/id #uuid "723d51be-6b3b-56b1-bcb4-95c843ad7ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "973eea0f-0399-52df-be30-a6a313feecd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370612} :answer-field/id #uuid "171e0f43-0b6f-50d8-acd4-b12cb3656332" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a00b6eac-5fc8-5d92-97e2-c15102a9bd04" :question/math-academy-id "q-163501" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=y-x.$ Find the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=-2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-(-2)|=|x+2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y-x)|x+2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y-x)(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y(x+2)^{2}-x(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}(x+2)^{2}-xy(x+2)^{2}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}(3-2x)(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}(-2{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+4x+12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{-{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}+12x]}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{3}+2+12)-(-8+\\frac{40}{3}+8-24)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((14-\\frac{13}{6})-(-24+\\frac{40}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{135}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a43d5434-d1f7-58c6-84d8-61594421e8be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370617} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6b6585-adfc-57a3-ae7b-7ce88ec212fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370618} {:answer/id #uuid "9b177870-5a68-534b-8de9-386f825eb02a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370619} {:answer/id #uuid "6456c51d-49f8-598c-881b-92ec921d481c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370620} {:answer/id #uuid "45c5a075-214f-53f2-b028-798c59213bbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a43d5434-d1f7-58c6-84d8-61594421e8be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370617} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cec18bb-5c6a-5cee-80c8-b9188f37c88f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61b80712-a863-5333-8bf7-6ae5efc36dbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-163563" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/74c26773d49442671fcf6526764215523ca0231a7889671330a7ac539f3402fc.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=2y$ and $x=3-y$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{6}.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{x}{2}\\le y\\le 3-x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/0c9efcbae53bdd2620b0bf7009ce4f4f2a20a38f393cac008899621ec391d261.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{3-x}(\\frac{y}{6})|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{3-x}(\\frac{y}{6})(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)[{\\int }_{x/2}^{3-x}\\frac{y}{6}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4){[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}]}_{x/2}^{3-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)[\\frac{(3-x)^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{48}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)(36-24x+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{4}-36{x}^{3}+144{x}^{2}-240x+144\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{80}-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{16}+{x}^{3}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+3x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{5}-3+8-10+6)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370622 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61c73ace-ef7f-5218-bd77-4565b76e7172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{48}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370624} {:answer/id #uuid "a46f2926-a4af-55a2-a995-c293befd5f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370625} {:answer/id #uuid "86f549a8-9269-53c5-8538-c985739c7e61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370626} {:answer/id #uuid "89b8f17e-460b-5f8d-b536-4b4f6fcd6ce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370627} {:answer/id #uuid "bc424605-14e0-59b2-9566-d4be70dd5954" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61c73ace-ef7f-5218-bd77-4565b76e7172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{48}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370624} :answer-field/id #uuid "c952dcfc-a287-59d9-b904-fd215324f412" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "527939a0-b082-5ef0-a084-bab058f7fe76" :question/math-academy-id "q-163568" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/55a781e535e1b469bc5da659eff8f82afd27a1e8bb92ccd36c2fce5a9dd49b07.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{4y}{3}$ and $x=4-\\frac{4y}{3}$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=2-x.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{3}{4}x\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{3}{4}x},\n$$\n\n \n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/1f332ebf554ac0e1b9e5099244aa50de0beef38c92efcba04e95e73abd21ecb6.png)\n\n    \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{3x/4}^{3-3x/4}(2-x)|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{3x/4}^{3-3x/4}{(2-x)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-x)^{3}[{\\int }_{3x/4}^{3-3x/4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-x)^{3}[y]_{3x/4}^{3-3x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-x)^{3}(3-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{3x}{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-x)^{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{[\\frac{(2-x)^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(0-\\frac{{2}^{5}}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c23a9e7-b376-5ce9-903d-f22766627096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370631} {:answer/id #uuid "c76e175b-53cf-5e26-8966-092d7c830164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370632} {:answer/id #uuid "a358a54d-ab57-5f14-9ef4-cd468cadcd51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370633} {:answer/id #uuid "333ec966-5d0f-5191-99cd-c33b62ea108c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370634} {:answer/id #uuid "abf82ae9-0a77-5908-8c1a-d784a1597a6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c23a9e7-b376-5ce9-903d-f22766627096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370631} :answer-field/id #uuid "c85fb12f-bfd2-5441-8a86-b4002fe1b771" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0eff1da-2e80-5041-8e31-1b867363164a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163583" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/2f847a5551c0bdc5aea20673814ba6eddc10daca7661cca2b2db76c953672225.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=y-1$ and $x=7-y$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y-1}{9}.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,x+1\\le y\\le 7-x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/b86b9a595786e544159e08fef12952c88e1bf9f796fb4ae3089e877dc9119b3f.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-3|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x+1}^{7-x}(\\frac{y-1}{9})|x-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x+1}^{7-x}(\\frac{y-1}{9})(x-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{7-x}\\frac{y-1}{9}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}{[\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{18}]}_{x+1}^{7-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[\\frac{(6-x)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[\\frac{12(3-x)}{18}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{[\\frac{(x-3)^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(0-\\frac{81}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3240086-930e-549a-8cf1-87e6407cc50b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370638} {:answer/id #uuid "89a916b5-917f-5c55-8ff7-b8aa2e4acf5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370639} {:answer/id #uuid "46c09183-8852-59da-86e9-88e0746cba5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370640} {:answer/id #uuid "6a98bf1a-90a9-56b9-ad86-e6e25d82b031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370641} {:answer/id #uuid "a0918678-451c-5145-acf5-427161556a78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46c09183-8852-59da-86e9-88e0746cba5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370640} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1a9dfc7-f4f2-5493-9e2c-a92510fa6ecd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f82c33cd-5fdb-59d6-9b46-1e4b0a7ea3b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163618" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{M}{4}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{M}{4}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}({\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}\\cdot [x]_{-1}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y-2)^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}(1-(-1))(\\frac{1}{3}(2-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(0-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(0-(-\\frac{8}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370643 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183f20e3-d2cd-5e5a-91c0-082547219098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{M}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370645} {:answer/id #uuid "55957380-5df5-5871-ac1a-67c48e9145bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370646} {:answer/id #uuid "d45ebd6c-1645-5abd-ab4a-232926879b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370647} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcc0e5c-9e20-5e1e-a14b-a7680825deb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370648} {:answer/id #uuid "e903cf5f-a042-5e9c-872c-0cec3cbeb4de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d45ebd6c-1645-5abd-ab4a-232926879b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370647} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b953e83-5ff4-5294-9290-1242fb7643bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1bd5086-46a3-54e4-b28e-039af25e92e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-163621" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 1=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{M}{3}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{M}{3}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}({\\int }_{2}^{5}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(x-2)^{3}]_{2}^{5}\\cdot {[y]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}(5-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(2-2)^{3})\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(9-0)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370650 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec9c4051-ca46-592f-80e2-03065ca2892f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370652} {:answer/id #uuid "c00efc82-ed21-5811-bca6-9652882403b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370653} {:answer/id #uuid "07377844-a68e-5bb4-8f82-91921c7e5f80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370654} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ad27b4-8a7e-54c8-83b3-352cba08164b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370655} {:answer/id #uuid "fe1578c8-a801-5bc5-bdf6-b022af24e92b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07377844-a68e-5bb4-8f82-91921c7e5f80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370654} :answer-field/id #uuid "f84654cf-b7ae-570b-909f-e6cdb3e736e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "15faa565-0737-5b72-a4a0-6585bf2a9f39" :question/math-academy-id "q-163622" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 2=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{M}{6}|x+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{M}{6}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}({\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(x+1)^{3}]_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(\\frac{1}{3}(2+1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(-1+1)^{3})\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(9-0)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d3b01e9-7201-5297-8a14-6bf87c905b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{M}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370659} {:answer/id #uuid "e2d72ec7-9238-574e-867a-32ec5502fcaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370660} {:answer/id #uuid "0f47fdde-671e-5e73-b947-458c5c33c2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370661} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a2caaf-a09f-53e1-a943-0caaf613017e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370662} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9f389f-757d-51b5-8ad7-3aaefbe8e921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f47fdde-671e-5e73-b947-458c5c33c2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370661} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c9af981-1610-50e9-8c37-71c6b96a8dab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dddb03a6-92c6-5454-bdcf-1c33144360e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-163626" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/cd19503a1b72cd353cd2bacad0c187a1f83881d511b6ffcf0e99755ab9f682a9.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y=x$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{1}{4},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/4463119c9f2ff0c1c658dd573add51a000cc50187e7dd59f39a40ba7c3abfce2.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=4M.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}[y]_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-2x+1)(x-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-2{x}^{2}+2{x}^{4}-{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4M(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{1}{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4820138b-483c-5ced-8df9-9849f5f2a7cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia Given a Description of a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95699bc2-35e0-55b1-b6ca-50dc7d18df04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64M}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370666} {:answer/id #uuid "341b8e29-7bb5-573e-9268-b7b1e236f116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{65M}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370667} {:answer/id #uuid "6182ac1e-166b-5fbe-b89f-b25d6fc15f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370668} {:answer/id #uuid "d330f42f-e24e-580c-a89a-99a5cad209d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{65M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370669} {:answer/id #uuid "0de9bcd0-f08c-504e-bebc-5445beb4dcd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6182ac1e-166b-5fbe-b89f-b25d6fc15f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370668} :answer-field/id #uuid "39bef840-01c9-5a46-b90f-558e659b455d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04daaed1-6376-5a28-ad01-61618bc0bbd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-163656" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its $x$-coordinate. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $y=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=kx,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}kx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =k(2-0)(3-0) \\\\  & =6k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=kx=\\frac{M}{6}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{M}{6}x|y+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{M}{6}x(y+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}({\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}(y+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y+1)^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(4-0)\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(64-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\frac{63}{3} \\\\  & =7M.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4820138b-483c-5ced-8df9-9849f5f2a7cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia Given a Description of a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63fdb99b-6ee2-5282-839d-35dd35e0e2cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370673} {:answer/id #uuid "41085348-4057-52c0-950f-1d31f7b07f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8M}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370674} {:answer/id #uuid "47684372-4425-5b77-bc86-81f8bcf76194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370675} {:answer/id #uuid "055e2f6a-5c20-5263-ac07-90a898f74e45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370676} {:answer/id #uuid "e3fd4d04-701e-5341-98a6-82e74bf02263" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "055e2f6a-5c20-5263-ac07-90a898f74e45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370676} :answer-field/id #uuid "8df614d9-7e07-5591-a7fb-c9179f189efb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "280fa22e-e2b1-5fb6-915d-588956a0f36b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163660" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}k{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot [x]_{-2}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}(2-(-2))(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2}=\\frac{3M}{4}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{4}{y}^{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{4}{y}^{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}({\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{4}-4{y}^{3}+4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot [x]_{-2}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}-{y}^{4}+\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot (2-(-2))\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}-1+\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\frac{8}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4820138b-483c-5ced-8df9-9849f5f2a7cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia Given a Description of a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb1975ce-b1d5-5689-8594-5aa3740b0587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28M}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370680} {:answer/id #uuid "9a592913-31f4-52d3-8add-8dd241aac5e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370681} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f76c27-4365-5094-817b-aafbbffffe87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370682} {:answer/id #uuid "b29aa1d2-e39e-58a5-bfbd-9544dbd3063a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10M}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370683} {:answer/id #uuid "03b5c57f-2baf-5224-8a5f-39fe88abe52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03b5c57f-2baf-5224-8a5f-39fe88abe52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370684} :answer-field/id #uuid "b82777e0-8fc2-54c7-8b2b-450e6b2f3999" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f9f537d-e887-50ce-a686-d0ca7e3b69ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-163669" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/aaa08372caf804751c80d37af49d0b27394dfe20b6d2dba6868a7739b4062921.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the lines $y=\\frac{x}{2},$ $y=x,$ and $x=1.$ \nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,\\frac{x}{2}\\le y\\le x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/84ec89a3f4d786fe387b33aacc3de7c013866387354897f785ff69f9d65437ad.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $y=0$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{x}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{x/2}^{x}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y]}_{x/2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=8M{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{x}8M{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{x/2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{24})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7{x}^{5}}{24}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7{x}^{5}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{18}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4820138b-483c-5ced-8df9-9849f5f2a7cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia Given a Description of a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78e7cbb8-6d90-51bb-b635-d30b0c104658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{M}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370687} {:answer/id #uuid "dc273650-c0ca-54e2-90e3-bc4582c48cba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370688} {:answer/id #uuid "78eb0560-a1e8-56ab-b0f1-d31d3570abde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370689} {:answer/id #uuid "a42d8952-8e04-549b-b393-33e207cb6beb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370690} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf1eece-059d-5952-b219-9a0ca32c6efc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3M}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc273650-c0ca-54e2-90e3-bc4582c48cba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370688} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6328258-2e64-5a3c-a863-5e9d3cf910b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1b65c72c-7c28-579f-b489-369412372954" :question/math-academy-id "q-163729" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/2e8eee199131d64b8772e15acb848030ac810cc96fd20b4f75005e5aab2770ed.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=4$ in the first quadrant.\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 2},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/f5a73161415455032a7fd2031dba8f1c56a7ccb40bf6dc3e4fa405a69aee74d8.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k|x|=kx,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}kx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}x[y]_{{x}^{2}}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4x-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{[2{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =k(8-4) \\\\  & =4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=kx=\\frac{M}{4}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}\\frac{M}{4}x\\cdot |y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}\\frac{M}{4}x\\cdot (y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x{[\\frac{(y-2)^{3}}{3}]}_{{x}^{2}}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{({x}^{2}-2)^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(8x-x({x}^{2}-2)^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(-{x}^{7}+6{x}^{5}-12{x}^{3}+16)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{[-\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}+{x}^{6}-3{x}^{4}+16x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}(-32+64-48+32) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
